#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060575} :activity/id #uuid "1f56b8ef-868f-57e2-ae40-b8e705105170" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050366 :topic/id #uuid "4264930a-5f20-54f0-ad2a-c3ad45c03658" :topic/math-academy-id 250} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060575 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060989 :tutorial/content "A **conditional statement** (or **implication**) is a mathematical statement that takes the form\n\n$\\qquad$ *$P$ implies $Q,$*\n\nor equivalently,\n\n$\\qquad$ *if $P,$ then $Q.$*\n\nSymbolically, it can be written as $P \\Rightarrow Q,$ where $P$ is called the **antecedent** (or **hypothesis**) and $Q$ is called the **consequent** (or **conclusion**).\n\nThe truth table for $P \\Rightarrow Q$ is shown below.\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\, P \\Rightarrow Q \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm T$ |\n\nIntuitively, an implication can be viewed as a \"promise\" that whenever $P$ is true, $Q$ is also true. The implication is true unless the promise is broken, i.e., $P$ is true, and $Q$ is false.\n\nWe'll discuss the intuition behind implications in more detail later in the lesson." :tutorial/id #uuid "a6598728-1780-50b5-af45-ace426318bc6" :tutorial/math-academy-id 7977 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "62e05d8d-2ee3-5cd5-8592-01e6eef66d71" :step/math-academy-id 154035 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060576}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060576 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059705 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059414 :question/id #uuid "8831a019-f252-5678-9855-6c0f1da89f77" :question/math-academy-id "e-12706"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "df9791a3-465d-57e4-8f2e-40fb9fb18d70" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060141} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060142} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376274} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376280} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376298} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376308}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Truth Values of Implications"} :step/id #uuid "89220a35-670a-5c3b-9161-aa844a949880" :step/math-academy-id 154036 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060577}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060577 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059706 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059413 :question/id #uuid "0b97d670-694b-52e5-aa55-1224985f83a8" :question/math-academy-id "e-12705"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e1c01fd-dea0-5761-9499-d622a34fea3e" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050783}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060143} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060157} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060158} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376394} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376407} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390077} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390119} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406982}] :knowledge-point/title "Completing a Truth Table With Compound Statements"} :step/id #uuid "cb82b9e6-f25a-5610-8374-2261c53cde3b" :step/math-academy-id 154039 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060578}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060578 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186061000 :tutorial/content "Let's recall the truth table for $P\\Rightarrow Q.$\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\, P \\Rightarrow Q \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm T$ |\n\nWe consider a concrete example to build further intuition behind the truth values in this table.\n\nSuppose your teacher promises that *if* you score at least $90$ on the exam, *then* you will receive an A. In other words, the teacher has promised that a score of at least $90$ on the exam implies that you will receive an A: $$\\textrm{Score at least 90} \\: \\Rightarrow \\: \\textrm{Receive an A}$$\n\nNow, the teacher may or may not be lying. The implication is true if the teacher tells the truth and false if the teacher lies.\n\nThe following four situations are possible:\n\n1. You score $90$ and receive an A. In this case, the teacher has told the truth. They have kept the promise. $\\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n2. You score $90$ and do *not* receive an A. In this case, the teacher has lied. They have broken the promise. $\\quad \\color{red}\\times$\n3. You do *not* score $90,$ yet you receive an A. In this case, the teacher has told the truth! The promise does not apply because you did not score at least $90.$ $\\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n4. You do *not* score $90$ and do *not* receive an A. Again, the teacher has told the truth. The promise does not apply because you did not score at least $90.$ $\\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\nEach of these situations corresponds to a row in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\textrm{At least 90}$ | $\\textrm{Receive an A}$ | $\\textrm{Score at least 90} \\Rightarrow \\textrm{Receive an A}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm T$ |" :tutorial/id #uuid "6943ab9c-bf27-5dbb-9871-a5647b7d3b74" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8292 :tutorial/title "Intuition Behind the Implication Truth Table"} :step/id #uuid "4b3b0e3b-bca5-585d-999e-a2ea88c36b2b" :step/math-academy-id 154043 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060579}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060579 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059707 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059412 :question/id #uuid "13e5834d-4d70-5893-a4bf-9927000d522d" :question/math-academy-id "e-12704"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64a3922f-7e74-562f-9bb9-c4a41e912ce7" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060417} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060423} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375637} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375693} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377871} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377878} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377885} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406980} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406981}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Conditional Statements"} :step/id #uuid "ea087540-046f-51b4-a818-16971088b6d6" :step/math-academy-id 154044}] :activity/title "Conditional Statements" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059934}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046679} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406984} :activity/id #uuid "e3bb9df3-04b6-5d77-8062-3bd56ac21bf2" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050366 :topic/id #uuid "4264930a-5f20-54f0-ad2a-c3ad45c03658" :topic/math-academy-id 250} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406983 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406980 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cfbb4fe-6765-539a-b1fe-a3a402299b48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406960} {:answer/id #uuid "6468d182-e5ca-52c7-91c5-873befcae9ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406962} {:answer/id #uuid "6faeed3c-4f73-5576-a69a-7f5fc255a52b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406964} {:answer/id #uuid "96783f0b-1578-5947-bf81-9015eff667e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406967} {:answer/id #uuid "f2c65aaf-1f1f-5a46-a0a8-cb5ff99c1cc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406972}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406964} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a77f2d5-b26b-5d52-b3a8-7c324acb6f02" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406978}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "55e540af-11e2-5ec3-9b47-ab0da3ac740e" :question/math-academy-id "q-103558" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- **If** $12$ is divisible by $3$, **then** $9$ is divisible by $4.$\n- **If** $5$ is divisible by $2$, **then** $10$ is divisible by $5.$\n- **If** $9$ is divisible by $5$, **then** $6$ is divisible by $3.$" :question/worked-solution "An implication $A⇒B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the \"promise\" is broken.\n\n- Statement I is false. The antecedent \"$12$ is divisible by $3$\" is true, and the consequent \"$9$ is divisible by $4$\" is false. So the promise is broken, and the statement is false.\n\n- Statement II is true. The antecedent \"$5$ is divisible by $2$\" is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\n- Statement III is true. Again, the antecedent \"$9$ is divisible by $5$\" is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} :step/id #uuid "52b92551-8e29-55f1-ae0e-36ee601e078e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406985}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406984 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406981 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c24a347-5951-5876-9f2d-8a1d7c5b9f75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406956} {:answer/id #uuid "383d59b8-a864-5389-8975-dc9bbacfa5e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406957} {:answer/id #uuid "5017cc1a-c69b-5371-9aff-5e273c1bbfe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406959} {:answer/id #uuid "9ca16a39-9404-5469-a817-d4f31a93d630" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406968} {:answer/id #uuid "ac3fcded-1928-518d-b875-ec2601c5af9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406970}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406957} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cad3447-1622-501b-827e-837284b22076" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406974}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "806aafe6-aa9d-53f3-a7d9-19809d388a29" :question/math-academy-id "q-82092" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- **If** $7$ is an even number, **then** $6$ is an odd number.\n- **If** $6$ is an even number, **then** $7$ is an even number.\n- **If** $6$ is an even number, **then** $7$ is an odd number." :question/worked-solution "An implication $A⇒B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the \"promise\" is broken.\n\n- Statement I is true. The antecedent \"$7$ is an even number\" is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\n- Statement II is false. The antecedent \"$6$ is an even number\" is true, and the consequent \"$7$ is an even number\" is false. So the promise is broken, and the statement is false.\n\n- Statement III is true. The antecedent \"$6$ is an even number\" is true, and the consequent \"$7$ is an odd number\" is true. So the promise is kept, and the statement is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} :step/id #uuid "c4e3aeea-5769-5fb5-81bc-48e1231cf682" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406983}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406985 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406982 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a334099-1f7f-5c0b-aead-371217a694de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406966} {:answer/id #uuid "a2888028-3901-5c34-ae8a-4a28ac3aca86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406969}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406969} :answer-field/id #uuid "2aee77f4-9be5-5c3a-80a1-10941ff43d8b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406975} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e14bb50-b52f-54ce-95fb-59ff76aadc0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406958} {:answer/id #uuid "f722b6c6-65d9-5629-96ce-1fb6fc2acbcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406973}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406973} :answer-field/id #uuid "5567147c-6f0e-52d8-9449-dc159b1a7899" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406976} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6931d52b-ab40-549d-8508-bab0ac42c5ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406963} {:answer/id #uuid "74e8728a-9112-5092-beaa-752dfc425e85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406965}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406963} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a198ffa-6bcf-5c46-8bb4-49b21b82a7a8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406977} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d6a50a3-bb24-530f-a62b-129c6bdb591b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406961} {:answer/id #uuid "e7a03093-15bd-5e22-b3ec-be4928468ac0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406971}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406961} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4032492-1493-553b-bc31-fe628a9c1050" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406979}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e0bd03cd-0c48-596c-b039-0f9c85a18c3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-182663" :question/problem "Find the missing values in the following truth table:" :question/worked-solution "First, we add columns for $¬P,$ $¬Q$ and $¬P∨¬Q:$\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬P\\,$ | $\\,¬Q\\,$ | $\\,¬P∨¬Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nNow, we add a column for $P⇒(¬P∨¬Q).$ This statement is true unless $P$ is true and $¬P∨¬Q$ is false. \n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬P\\,$ | $\\,¬Q\\,$ | $\\,¬P∨¬Q\\,$ | $\\,P⇒(¬P∨¬Q)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |"} :step/id #uuid "ebbb7ea7-a0d0-5fb6-9455-eb7f19b0c1b3"}] :activity/title "Conditional Statements" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406955}]}
